+When using HTTP/2, Fastify writes large string and buffer payloads in smaller
+chunks so that a cancelled request does not affect the rest of the session.
+Stream payloads are written as emitted, so applications serving HTTP/2 should
+make sure their streams emit reasonably sized chunks (e.g. 64 KiB or less)
+instead of a single large chunk.
